    "durationMs": 278140,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and fully tested.\n\n**Implementation** — `src/main.rs` (axum 0.8.4 + sqlx 0.8 against PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL`):\n- `POST /links` — validates url (absolute http/https with host, stored/returned exactly as submitted), optional custom code (4-20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`), auto-generates 8-char codes with collision retry. Returns 201 `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}`, 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 on bad input.\n- `GET /links/{code}` — 200 with link JSON, 404 `{\"error\":...}` for unknown codes.\n- `GET /r/{code}` — `UPDATE ... RETURNING url` in one atomic statement: 302 + `Location`, incrementing clicks exactly once; 404 for unknown.\n- `GET /links` — `{\"items\":[...],\"total\":n}` ordered by ascending creation id.\n- Malformed JSON (parsed manually from raw body so every rejection maps uniformly), missing/invalid url, and invalid code all return 422 `{\"error\":...}`.\n\n**Persistence** — `migrations/0001_create_links.sql` creates the `links` table; migrations are applied on startup before binding the port, so `sh start.sh` (which runs `cargo run --release` in the foreground on 0.0.0.0:8000) always applies pending migrations first. Nothing is installed in start.sh; dependencies are already built in `target/release`.\n\n**Verified** — 37 HTTP checks passed: create (auto + custom codes), duplicate → 409, all invalid url/code/malformed-JSON cases → 422, redirect → 302 with correct `Location` and exactly-once click increments, list ordering/total, and a full server restart confirming links and click counts survive. README includes the start instructions.\n\nThe test server is stopped and port 8000 is free — the API is ready for `sh start.sh`."
